  "notes": "Not yet flown per Launch Library (0 launches recorded). Weekly maintenance 2026-08-10: Shetland News/Shetland Times report RFA de-stacked the vehicle from the SaxaVord pad on an unspecified issue found during hot-fire test prep, and SaxaVord put the temporary traffic regulation orders for the prior five-week window on hold pending a new application; the LL2 NET (2026-08-31) was not overwritten (single press source, no replacement date stated) but recorded as a disputed.competing null claim. LL2 was rate-limited this run; recheck next run. Weekly maintenance 2026-08-20: LL2 rate-limited again (429 on first call this run, stopped per budget rule). The prior on-file NET of 2026-08-31 is now confirmed superseded: wide, independently corroborating reporting (SpaceNews 'Tank problem delays first RFA launch', Space.com, IET Engineering and Technology, Aviation Week, Shetland News, orbital-intel.com) states RFA announced July 28 it destacked the vehicle after a pad issue, and SaxaVord canceled the reserved Aug-Sept launch window outright; no replacement NET has been announced and outlets describe a possible slip into late 2026. next_flight_date nulled accordingly (source proving the prior date wrong); disputed.competing removed since both the old competing claim and the new finding now agree on 'no confirmed date'.",
